course: dictionary
lesson: 11872
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The clues in the sentence tell you which meaning is right. Read the words around the word first, then choose the meaning that fits.
explain: «The bouncer at the door checked everyone's age before letting them in.» The door and the checking show that a bouncer is a person who guards a club or bar. Try your meaning in the sentence to be sure it makes sense.
explain: «The bowler sent a fast bouncer past the batter's head.» The bowler, the batter and the fast ball are clues from cricket, so a bouncer here is a ball that bounces high near the batter's head. «Mum put the baby in the bouncer, and she giggled.» The baby is the clue: a bouncer can be a seat that bounces a baby.
fact: A bouncer is a person who stands at the door of a club or bar, checks who comes in and removes people who cause trouble.
fact: In cricket, a bouncer is a fast ball that bounces high, near the batter's head.
fact: A baby bouncer is a seat or swing that bounces a baby.
fact: One word can have several meanings, so always check the context.
fact: «Bouncer» is a noun: one bouncer, two bouncers.
exercise: «The bouncer asked to see my ID before I went in.» What is a bouncer in this sentence? | A baby seat that bounces | *A person who checks who comes into a club | A type of dance | A fast ball in cricket
exercise: «The bowler's bouncer rose high above the batter's head.» What does bouncer mean here? | A person at the door | *A fast ball that bounces high | A swing for babies | A bouncy castle
exercise: «The baby giggled in her bouncer while Dad made funny faces.» Which meaning fits best? | A big tough man | A club door guard | *A seat that bounces a baby | A cricket ball
test: Chloe said, «Keep the baby happy in the bouncer.» What is a bouncer in this sentence? | *A seat that bounces a baby | A dog | A cricket ball | A door guard at a club
test: «Two bouncers stood at the door, looking very serious.» What do the bouncers do? | Bowl fast balls at the batter | Dance on the stage | *Check who comes in and remove trouble-makers | Rock babies to sleep
exam: Which meaning of bouncer fits «The bouncer threw the rude man out of the bar»? | *A person who removes people who cause trouble | A baby seat | A bouncy ball | A cricket ball
